e\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7b3af1349e6a2449419067c639ca12448b74d41089b507ebf38d112fc7bb4ec5","event_uuid":"60627e4e-f3c6-4b7d-98e7-3c425314ee07","position":{"commit_sha":"a9655ee8e6c6a8badc3d2882e17b49f1f590ae12","position":"1786575748816541001-60627e4e-f3c6-4b7d-98e7-3c425314ee07"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"929157d987ffcf2a0fef9c5d60617dc606baf0c374ba7cce5f0d29684766d4f0","event_uuid":"6803b755-1a9f-41d4-bb2e-9e8dfee24e11","position":{"commit_sha":"573585f8f31684b2f9c745d130fe416207251436","position":"1786576360523331001-6803b755-1a9f-41d4-bb2e-9e8dfee24e11"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"78c3671e805f8708dd1853081168ed6d5e2787b5c3f57dfffae9d055c03fc7e3","event_uuid":"13ab845b-71fa-497c-8ada-a3603aa33284","position":{"commit_sha":"5d02eef74b3f3c827d95aeaa522425894e615786","position":"1786576894496066083-13ab845b-71fa-497c-8ada-a3603aa33284"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 1687 pushed for review (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1687), commit 1dce563bcc.\n\nImplemented: DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX 1800 -> 2400 (infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh), the pinned test tightened from >= 1.0x to >= 2.0x DEFAULT_REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS via a named DEFER_BOUND_REVIEW_CAP_MULTIPLE constant (test updated, not deleted), and the restated 1800s cadence figure in monitoring_autodeploy.tf corrected. Local gates: pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py 13 passed; terraform fmt -check + validate pass; make lint clean.\n\nPROVENANCE NOTE, recorded so the decision is not later mistaken for a tracker-native one: the approval to raise the bound reached me through the operator dispatch, NOT as a written approval in the store. The lorikeet sweep (b902-18af-14ed-4da1 comment 12) recorded this as one of two items 'surfaced for operator decision'. It also runs AGAINST piranha's (7b4a-0f39-1a45-4ce9) closed disposition, which said 'I would not raise the bound' on the strength of a saturated-episode trace where in_flight oscillated 2 -> 1 -> 2 and never reached 0 for 30 minutes.\n\nBoth the code comment and the test docstring state that tension explicitly rather than papering over it: 2400s absorbs the four 10-130s overshoots the Aug-12 markers actually show, and does NOT fix a saturated episode, against which a larger bound only defers the same kill. Whether the Aug-12 episodes were saturated is unestablished -- comment 12 presents terminal markers only, no per-episode in_flight traces. The residual concurrency-gauge-vs-single-review-timer finding stays open on 7b4a's chain.\n\nNo operator apply needed for this ticket: the terraform edit is comment-only, so plan is a no-op.","timestamp":1786576360523331001}],"created_at":1786575326175780001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ac13b360-cdde-4716-9b49-db234bd58abc","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7b4a-0f39-1a45-4ce9"},{"link_uuid":"13ab845b-71fa-497c-8ada-a3603aa33284","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6f61-ba69-e103-42ed"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nAll four `AUTODEPLOY_REVIEW_INTERRUPT` / `bound-exceeded` firings on 2026-08-12 missed the\n`DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX` bound by a hair: `deferred_for` = 1810s, 1820s, 1810s, 1930s against a\n1800s bound — overshoots of 10s, 20s, 10s and 130s. Each one killed an in-flight LLM-Review\n(the backfill reconciler retries it, but the gate stalls meanwhile), and they fired at ~10x\nthe normal rate during a 60+-merge landing burst. The bound is sized for a steady-state\nreview queue and is marginally too small for a burst; a bound that misses by 10s buys nothing\nthat a slightly larger bound would not have caught for free.\n\n## Where it lives\n\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:70-82` — the rationale comment + `DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX=\"${DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX:-1800}\"`.\n  Commit 34cd pinned 1800s as **1.5x** `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (`DEFAULT_REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\n  = 1200`, `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:31`).\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py:399-420` —\n  `test_defer_bound_default_outlasts_the_apps_own_per_review_cap` reads the shell default out of\n  the script and asserts it against the app constant, so the two cannot drift. It currently pins\n  the weaker `bound >= 1x` relationship.\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:133` — an alarm-cadence comment restating `1800s`.\n\n## Decision\n\nRaise the default to **2400s = 2.0x `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`**, and tighten the pinned test from\n`>= 1x` to `>= 2x` so the new relationship is enforced rather than merely commented.\n\nWhy 2400 and not more: 2400s clears the worst observed overshoot (1930s) by 470s — ~3.6x the\n130s miss — so all four firings would have deferred to completion. Why bounded at all: the\nsaturated-trace analysis on `greasy-plucky-piranha` showed that under *sustained* pipelining an\nunbounded raise does not prevent the kill, it only defers it, while a deploy that never lands\nis its own outage. Anchoring the bound to a fixed multiple of the app's own per-review cap keeps\nit self-adjusting (raising `REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` drags the bound with it, enforced by the\ntest) instead of being a free-floating literal.\n\nNo terraform resource changes — the terraform edit here is comment-only, so nothing in this\nticket requires an operator apply.\n\n## The counter-argument, and why the raise is still bounded\n\n`greasy-plucky-piranha` (7b4a-0f39-1a45-4ce9) closed with an explicit \"I would not raise the\nbound\". Its trace of the 03:03:04Z episode showed `in_flight` oscillating 2 -> 1 -> 2 and\n**never reaching 0 across 30 continuous minutes**: no single review outlived\n`REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, the bound was outlasted by ordinary *pipelining*. Under that\nsaturation a larger bound only defers the same kill. Tonight's sweep (`childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet`\nb902-18af-14ed-4da1, comment 12) presents only the terminal markers, not per-episode `in_flight`\ntraces, so whether the four Aug-12 episodes were saturated the same way is **unestablished**.\n\nThis ticket therefore does not claim to fix saturated episodes. It claims the narrower thing the\ndata does support: four firings missed by 10-130s, and a bound at 2.0x rather than 1.5x the\nper-review cap absorbs those margins. Where an episode really is saturated, 2400s defers the kill\nby 600s and no more — which is precisely why the raise is a fixed multiple of the app's cap and\nnot an unbounded one. The underlying residue piranha carried forward (34cd's rationale treats a\n*concurrent gauge* as if it were a single-review timer) is NOT closed by this ticket and remains\nopen on 7b4a's discovered_from chain.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py -q` — the pinned-relationship test and the\n  full drain suite (the burst/bound scenarios drive the real script).\n- `terraform fmt -check` + `terraform validate` in `infra/terraform` (comment-only change, but the\n  gates still run).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX` default is `2400` in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:82`, its rationale\n      comment rewritten to state the 2.0x relationship and cite the 2026-08-12 overshoot data\n      (1810/1820/1810/1930s against a 1800s bound). Checked: `grep DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX:- infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`.\n- [ ] `test_defer_bound_default_outlasts_the_apps_own_per_review_cap` asserts\n      `bound >= 2 * DEFAULT_REVIEW_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` — updated deliberately, not deleted — with the\n      docstring carrying the rationale. Checked:\n      `pytest tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py -q` passes.\n- [ ] The restated `1800s` figure in `infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf:133` reads 2400s.\n      Checked: `terraform fmt -check` + `terraform validate` pass; no resource attribute changes,\n      so `terraform plan` is a no-op and **no operator apply is required for this ticket**.\n- [ ] Change lands on `main` through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"raise the DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX default to 2400 and rewrite its rationale comment"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py","reason":"tighten the pinned bound/review-cap relationship from >=1x to >=2x"},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf","reason":"comment-only: correct the restated 1800s cadence figure"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6f61-ba69-e103-42ed"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7a626781-26a0-4ad8-9df7-5bb3fc11d239","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"594d-9b76-ede5-46ac","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Raise the autodeploy deferral bound to 2x the review cap","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0635a51e-def2-46dc-a94c-468af6ceeb95","ac13b360-cdde-4716-9b49-db234bd58abc","93434f93-b36b-4987-85a6-3b4dc10e68d4","0a7bd6c1-2255-4db6-8d18-3e824aaf3a39","7a626781-26a0-4ad8-9df7-5bb3fc11d239","db5574a4-2372-4981-9541-40055f5ca296","938342cf-3131-434a-a56f-6110de7eb8fb","60627e4e-f3c6-4b7d-98e7-3c425314ee07","6803b755-1a9f-41d4-bb2e-9e8dfee24e11","13ab845b-71fa-497c-8ada-a3603aa33284"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786576894496066084,"uuid":"f13d2a5b-202b-47dd-a9c4-04af415e7d63"}